* mkstemp.a - temp-name generator for the OS-9 backend.
* OS-9 has no atomic create-and-open temp primitive, and the stock c3 library
* has only mktemp().  exec/c3.c calls mkstemp(template) purely to fill the
* trailing XXXXX of the template in place (it ignores the return value), so we
* defer to mktemp(), which does exactly that (returns the name pointer in D).
 psect mkstemp_a,0,0,0,0,0
mkstemp:
 lbra mktemp            fill template in place; mktemp's result is returned
 endsect
